---
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro'; 
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import GSoCImage from '~/assets/logos/gsoc.png';
---


<PageLayout title="Google Summer of Code (GSoC)">
  <main class="mt-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto">
      <div class="flex justify-center my-6 pb-6">
        <div class="card p-4 w-full max-w-3xl shadow-xl">
          <Image src={GSoCImage} alt="GSoC logo" class="mx-auto mb-4" />
          <div class="card-body d-flex flex-column align-items-center light-mode">
            <div class="card-text">
              <p>
                Through the NumFOCUS organisation, equadratures participates in the Google Summer of Code.
                This programme seeks to involve undergraduate students in the development of open-source
                tools. Individual equadratures’ projects are designed to empower students with useful
                mathematical and statistical machinery, while helping the broader user community. Students
                are mentored by our development team and encouraged at each step of the GSOC programme.
              </p>
              <br />
              <p>Our past students are listed below:</p>
              <ul class="mt-4 text-left list-disc pl-5">
                <li>
                  <strong>2020</strong> Barney Hill <br />
                  Polynomial regression trees with orthogonal polynomials.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong>2021</strong> Simardeep Singh Sethi <br />
                  Developing an app for uncertainty quantification using polynomial chaos methods.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</PageLayout>
